{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  input %x: float\n  output %out: float (stored to; its values are listed after the run)\nsimplify: 15 SPIR-V instructions, 0 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 0 dead instructions removed\n  integer arithmetic cost under gt1030 (each instruction once): 0 -> 0\n  nothing to rewrite: no cheaper form of an integer instruction could be proved\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\nfloat simplify: 1 rewrite of float instructions applied, each with a derivation (no sampling)\n  reference: IEEE binary32, round to nearest even; pow, exp2, log2 correctly rounded (long double, then f32); NaN payloads ignored, -0 and +0 distinct; GLSL's undefined results (pow of x < 0, log2 of x <= 0 ...) may become anything\n  float cost under gt1030 (each component counted; step = compare + select, mix = subtract + fma): 3 -> 1 (-66.7%)\n  rewrites, the largest savings first:\n    %a = OpFDiv %float %x %float_3_0\n      -> %a = OpFMul %float %x %ucas_float_3eaaaaab\n      (divide by a constant as a multiply; -2)\n      proof: within the original's Vulkan precision (derived), not bit-exact\n        k = fl(1/3) = 0.33333334; k*d = 1 + delta with delta = 2.98e-08 (k*d is exact in double)\n          x*k = (x/d)(1 + delta), so |fl(x*k) - x/d| <= ulp/2 + |x/d| |delta| < (0.5 + 2^24 |delta|) ulp = 1 ulp (|v| < 2^24 ulp(v); subnormal results alike)\n          x/d correctly rounded is within 0.5 ulp, and both are floats: they differ by at most 1 ulp\n          Vulkan OpFDiv: 2.5 ulp (for |y| in [2^-126, 2^126]); the multiply is correctly rounded: 1 <= 2.5, so it is within the precision the division already had\n        not bit-exact: x = 3.0000005: / 3 gives 1.0000001, * 0.33333334 gives 1.0000002 (the quotient within |delta| of a rounding midpoint)\n        bound against the reference: 1 ulp\n  (nofile: simpl